This add-on comes unchanged from Dr. Du's SEED-Emulator repository:

    tools/InternetMap2/plugin/submit_event/

It is the add-on his Morris worm and Mirai demos use to show infected
machines on the Internet Map. With it installed, a machine calls

    bash /map-plugins/submit_event.sh -a flash        (or highlight, or restore)

and the map flashes that machine. The map's server looks for this folder at
/usr/src/app/plugin/submit_event inside itself; the examples put it there
when the lab is built, so it only has to be switched on:

    curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
         -d '{"name": "submit_event"}' http://localhost:8082/api/v1/install
